-- Calendar example: business days, public holidays and deadlines that roll
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT calendar

-- A day is a number: the count of days from 1 January 0000, which
-- DATE_SERIAL (YMD ...) works out. Sat 31 Oct 2026 is a Saturday; Mon 2 Nov
-- 2026 is treated as a public holiday below.
DECIDE `Mon 26 Oct` IS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 26)
DECIDE `Fri 30 Oct` IS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 30)
DECIDE `Sat 31 Oct` IS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 10 31)
DECIDE `Mon 2 Nov`  IS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 2)
DECIDE `Tue 3 Nov`  IS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 3)

-- A calendar on which Mon 2 Nov 2026 is a holiday
DECIDE `this year's calendar` IS `weekdays except the dates` (LIST YMD 2026 11 2)

-- The day itself if it is a business day, else the next one
#ASSERT `next business day on or after` `weekdays only` `Sat 31 Oct` EQUALS `Mon 2 Nov`
#ASSERT `next business day on or after` `weekdays only` `Mon 2 Nov` EQUALS `Mon 2 Nov`
#ASSERT `next business day on or after` `this year's calendar` `Sat 31 Oct` EQUALS `Tue 3 Nov`

-- Strictly after, even from a business day: one business day later
#ASSERT `add business days` `weekdays only` 1 `Fri 30 Oct` EQUALS `Mon 2 Nov`

-- Back to the Friday
#ASSERT `previous business day on or before` `weekdays only` `Sat 31 Oct` EQUALS `Fri 30 Oct`

-- Modified Following: rolling forward would leave October, so roll back
#ASSERT `modified following business day` `weekdays only` `Sat 31 Oct` EQUALS `Fri 30 Oct`

-- Two business days after Friday, skipping the weekend and the holiday
#ASSERT `add business days` `this year's calendar` 2 `Fri 30 Oct` EQUALS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 4)

-- The DATE forms give back a DATE
#EVAL `next business day on or after` `weekdays only` (YMD 2026 10 31)

-- `weekdays only` takes Saturday and Sunday as the weekend. For a country
-- whose weekend is Friday and Saturday, write the calendar out:
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sunday to Thursday` d MEANS
    NOT (`Weekday of` d EQUALS Friday OR `Weekday of` d EQUALS Saturday)

-- Fri 30 Oct is not a business day there; Sun 1 Nov is
#ASSERT `next business day on or after` `Sunday to Thursday` `Fri 30 Oct` EQUALS DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 11 1)

-- A deadline that rolls: pay five days after the notice, or on the next
-- business day if the fifth day is not one
DECLARE Party  IS ONE OF Seller, Buyer
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    notify HAS day IS A NUMBER
    pay

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Action
`pay within five days of notice` MEANS
    PARTY Seller MUST notify d WITHIN 10
    HENCE PARTY Buyer MUST pay WITHIN 0 OF (`next business day on or after` `this year's calendar` (d PLUS 5))

-- the fifth day, Sat 31 Oct, rolls past the weekend and the holiday to Tue 3 Nov
#TRACE `pay within five days of notice` AT `Mon 26 Oct` WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES notify `Mon 26 Oct` AT `Mon 26 Oct`
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT `Tue 3 Nov`
